<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Prismatic controlled comparison (full results). <math id="A3.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\text{LLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\text{LLM}}</annotation></semantics></math> = change from adapter to LLM-final. Top: text-describable attributes (named in captions). Bottom: non-textual attributes (object count, average object size, spatial spread; derived from annotations, not captions). Text baseline accuracy is substantially lower (.415–.495) for non-textual attributes, confirming their visual nature. Same architecture, same LLM, only encoder differs.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The mode alignment spectrum (Table <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix C Additional figures ‣ Modality Collapse as Mismatched Decoding: Information-Theoretic Limits of Multimodal LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) reveals which directions carry the mismatch. For each model, we decompose the adapter output covariance into eigenmodes and measure their text alignment. The dominant eigenmode is modality-specific (<math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\alpha}\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\alpha}\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>) for all non-text-aligned encoders, while for SigLIP even the dominant mode is text-aligned (<math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\alpha}=0.83" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0.83</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\alpha}=0.83</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T11" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T11.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
